      "item_body": "<p>[A]</p><p>Lorianne is studying for two different exams. Because of the nature of the courses, the measure of study effectiveness on a scale from 0 to 10 for the first course is E_1 = 0.6(9 + te^(-t/20)), while the measure for the second course is E_2 = 0.5(10 + te^(-t/10)), where each t is the time spent on that course. Lorianne is prepared to spend up to 30 h, in total, studying for the exams. The total effectiveness is given by f(t) = E_1 + E_2. How should this time be allocated to maximize total effectiveness?</p>",
      "user_response_type": "Text",
      "interaction_type": {
